    "media:imagetext": "-3-\nThanksgiving this year fell on the fifth anniversary of the\nSeeshan interlude.\nIn token of the special occasion for real\ngiving of thanks, we had the rummils over for dinner.\nWhile the\nfact was not mentioned by either of us, I am sure at\n• least two\nsilent toasts were drunk to you on\nthat occasion. I am sure I\nhave remarked to you many times that that experience was one I\nwouldn't take a pot of gold for; but at the same time, one I\nwouldn't willing repeat for the same amount. We all - that is\nDamaris, the Pecks, and I - look back on it now pleasantly as\ngratefully. The Pecks have a delightful and enviable\nfaculty of recalling all the enjoyable aspects and circumstances\nof things which have happened in the past.\nMuch of this has been\nimparted to me.\nAccordingly,\nthe Seeshan\naffair seems now more\nthan ever belore the greatest and most impressive of all the\nunusual near-tragic, but comic, things that have come our way.\nViewed from my side of the association, I praise the day I\ndecided to make a bid for a connection with Pan American. While\nConsular work was pleasant and extremely interesting, and\nalthough my associates, both superior and subordinate, left\nnothing to be asked for, my decision to change would be unaltered\nif I had it to do over again.\nYou will probably recall that I\nwas pretty enthusiastic about aviation before I came with the\nCompany•\nI was perhaps a little fanatically so. Analizing my\npresent feelings on the subject, I think that in all probability\nI am just as interested and enthusiastic, but that my interest\nand enthusiasm are \"growing up\". At any\nrate, I hope so, for I\nam confident that il I can retain their force\nand then direct\nthat force along the correct channels, a worthwhile dividend will\naccrue. In a few more days I will have completed my second year\nwith the Company, and viewing my present assignment in the light\nof what I have learned during that time, I fully realize how\nvery fortunate I am.\nIn the first place, Mr. Snyder lacks nothing\nas an immediate chief.\nThis is of course apart from our relations\nthe office.\nDamaris and I have come to know Mrs. Snyder\nand him. Knowing as you do, the people we left behind in China,\nI am sure you will understand what I wish to say when I remark\nthat the Snyders measure up in all respects.\nYour comment respecting the Pecks coincides in every way the\nextra-family leeling I hold for them.\nThe respect and regard you\nentertain for the Pecks is fully reciprocated, I can assure you\non unimpeachable authority, and I know also that they both hold a\nreal affection for \"the Bixbys\".\nTo speak in my own behalf on\nthis score would be merely superfluous!\nI apologize for having gone to such lengths with this.\nI am\nwell aware of the demands made on your time by the duties\nDivision \"sponsor\", I do not therefore,\nexpect that you will be\nable (or wish) to give this more than a hasty perusal; similarly,\nwe 11 look forward to your next letter,\nbut will not expect it\nuntil it turns up in the mail some morning.\nOur very best regards to you all.\nVery sincerely,\nwensures,\nCopied excerpt(in duplicate).\nTown\no oral ISI POS",
